  did #"actor brought into scope as the eleventh term (def/actor.md: minted anew at every discontinuity, compaction included, as a new actor with a source; a record of its own: model and prompt attested, three orientations as warrants earned by checks, consortia as references, experience computed; standing as a gate a dimension's producer declares over that record; subtypes mind and instrument); act gains by and concerns-actor relations and reading as attested-or-checked per producer with the check the default for a possibly-compacted mind; dimension may be of an actor and its producer reads the actor's record; disc-actor segment written; outline, README and counts updated"#
  why #"Joseph, 2026-11-09: a compaction is not a new version of an actor but a new, often confused and deceived actor starting with a summary of varying fidelity; the frontier/checkpoint separation gives orientation a purpose vivarium had to guess at; his list of what an actor is (state of the store and intended role above the line; LLM, system prompt, v2/domain/segment orientation, consortia, experience below) ending in "standing?"; and his decision that the mind belongs in scope since the act is central and verisectoria are in practice very concerned with the minds that turn over. The research read at msc/scratch/research-vivarium-heat-orientation-2026-11-09.md is the evidence."#
}

entry at="2026-11-09T15:10-07:00" by="Fable 5.1 session, at Joseph's correction, after reading both research reports whole" {
  did #"disc-actor and actor rewritten so the body states the design and names no other project as argument; what they were adjudicated against moved to Working Notes. From the live_docs read, working notes added where it bears on a term (reference: whether acyclicity belongs to the capping kind rather than to dependence in general; detection of unwritten references as the practical gap; expected references declared on the kind; deriving reference kinds by behaviour; kind: expected references as a kind-level declaration; segment: sources never rewritten, churn as a grain detector, restates agrees with the owner; frontier: completeness bounded by references, must be shown where changesets open and close, marks are not locks; actor: the steward's word written by proxy with a required reference, as a decision for Joseph) and one invariant to checkpoint: an acceptance warrants nothing about content, silence is not ratification. msc/notes/00-INDEX.md carries the correction that three live_docs behaviours the notes inherited were proposals."#
  why "Joseph, 2026-11-09: core-2 is the core model and should not reference live_docs or anything else as provenance; text changes only because the design changed, and the estate's own experience is reason enough for signer not author and the like. Provenance belongs in working notes and this log."
}

